# Standard-library stubs: utils package.
#
# Declaration-only stub file (`.Rtypes`); see base.Rtypes for the format. Side-effecting helpers get a
# precise `NULL` return; those whose result shape mirrors their input stay `Any` until the
# generic-vector design lands. Stubbing every name still makes it resolve and keeps strict mode quiet.

# widened to Any: the result is a prefix/suffix of the argument, so its shape mirrors the input. This is
# the shape-mirroring group; a `T[]`-over-a-type-variable return is deferred (see
# `.agents/memory/typing-design.md`), so a concrete return type would be falsely precise.
head : Any
tail : Any

# Side-effecting helpers: the value produced is not statically interesting, but the return type is a
# precise `NULL` (each returns `invisible(NULL)`). A bare leading positional plus `...` matches the
# working `sprintf`/`format` shape; the checker fills a variadic function's named parameters by name
# only, so a named leading parameter would reject the positional call.
str : fn(Any, ...: Any) -> NULL
write.csv : fn(Any, ...: Any) -> NULL
install.packages : fn(Any, ...: Any) -> NULL
help : fn(object: Any) -> NULL

# widened to Any: the result mirrors the input's structure. `read.csv` returns a data frame (no
# `data.frame` type yet); `modifyList` returns the argument list with its element structure changed, so
# a concrete return type would be falsely precise.
read.csv : Any
modifyList : Any
